{"claims":[{"excerpt":"## Uitgevouwen, maar nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap","claim":"Webb’s deployment was complete before it was ready for routine science.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures ... This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie, maar was niet hetzelfde als klaar zijn voor routinewetenschap","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The title’s contrast is consistent with the source’s timeline: Webb reached its fully deployed configuration in week two, while routine science began after six months.","materiality":"Central framing; accurately distinguishes deployment from readiness for routine science."},{"excerpt":"Webb moest opgevouwen in de kuip van de Ariane 5 passen: in zijn operationele configuratie was de telescoop daarvoor te groot.","claim":"Webb had to be folded to fit in the Ariane 5 fairing because its operational configuration was too large to fit there.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's fully deployed operational configuration is far too large to fit into any available rocket so it was designed to fold into a compact launch configuration that fit inside the Ariane 5.","narrative":"Webb moest compact in de Ariane 5-raket passen, hoewel zijn operationele configuratie daarvoor te groot was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source specifically says Webb folded into a compact configuration to fit inside the Ariane 5 fairing. “Kuip” refers to the fairing in this context.","materiality":"Provides accurate design context for why deployment was necessary."},{"excerpt":"Het bereiken van die configuratie vereiste een uitvouwing met veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten.","claim":"Reaching Webb’s operational configuration required a complex deployment with many steps and possible points of failure.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"There were over 50 major deployment steps, with 178 release mechanisms that had to perform perfectly or any one of over 300 single points of failure could have diminished or crippled the mission.","narrative":"De uitvouwing omvatte veel stappen en mogelijke faalpunten, waardoor duidelijk is dat dit een risicovolle fase was.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source documents more than 50 deployment steps and over 300 possible single points of failure; the piece summarizes these without claiming that a failure occurred.","materiality":"Conveys the documented complexity and stakes without changing the outcome."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing verliep soepel.","claim":"Webb’s deployment proceeded smoothly.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Webb's deployment was completed with remarkable smoothness.","narrative":"de uitvouwing verliep soepel.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This is a direct paraphrase of the source’s description of the deployment.","materiality":"Material context: it rules out an implication that later commissioning was recovery from a deployment failure."},{"excerpt":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld.","claim":"By the second week after launch, Webb’s mirrors had been unfolded and latched into place.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"During the second week after launch, we finished deploying the telescope structures by unfolding and latching the secondary mirror tripod and rotating and latching the two primary mirror wings.","narrative":"In de tweede week waren de spiegels uitgevouwen en vergrendeld","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source specifies the secondary mirror tripod and both primary-mirror wings; the piece accurately summarizes these as the mirrors being unfolded and latched.","materiality":"Identifies the second-week deployment milestone."},{"excerpt":"Webb had daarmee zijn operationele configuratie bereikt","claim":"The second-week unfolding and latching brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration.","narrative":"De uitvouwing bracht de telescoop in de tweede week in die configuratie","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source explicitly connects completion of the second-week telescope deployments with reaching the fully deployed operational configuration.","materiality":"Establishes what the deployment milestone achieved."},{"excerpt":"maar was nog niet klaar voor routinewetenschap.","claim":"Reaching the fully deployed operational configuration did not mean Webb was ready for routine science.","category":"outcome","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments. ... After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"maar was niet hetzelfde als klaar zijn voor routinewetenschap","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source places optics alignment, instrument calibration, and the start of routine science after deployment was complete.","materiality":"This is the piece’s central distinction and is directly supported by the source."},{"excerpt":"Tijdens de ingebruikname volgden weken van afkoeling, maanden van spiegeluitlijning en daarna de kalibratie van de instrumenten.","claim":"During commissioning, Webb underwent several weeks of cooling, months of mirror alignment, and then instrument calibration.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"The telescope and scientific instruments started to cool rapidly ... but it took several weeks for them to cool all the way down and reach stable temperatures. ... In the second, third and fourth months: Initial optics checkouts, and telescope alignment. ... In the fifth and sixth months: Calibration and completion of commissioning.","narrative":"Daarna volgden weken van afkoeling, maanden van spiegeluitlijning en instrumentkalibratie.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source describes several weeks of cooldown in the first month, telescope alignment in months two through four, and instrument calibration in months five and six. The piece preserves that broad sequence.","materiality":"Summarizes the post-deployment commissioning stages and their order."},{"excerpt":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","claim":"Webb began routine science operations after six months.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"After six months: “Science operations!” Webb began its science mission and started to conduct routine science operations.","narrative":"Na zes maanden begon Webb aan routinewetenschap.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"This matches the source’s stated endpoint of the six-month commissioning period.","materiality":"Supplies the timeline endpoint and distinguishes it from the earlier deployment milestone."},{"excerpt":"De uitvouwing was dus een belangrijke mijlpaal, maar niet het einde van de ingebruikname.","claim":"Deployment was an important milestone, but commissioning continued afterward.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"This brought Webb into its fully deployed operational configuration. ... The remaining five months of commissioning were all about aligning the optics and calibrating the scientific instruments.","narrative":"Daarmee maakt de tijdlijn het onderscheid duidelijk tussen de voltooide uitvouwing en het afronden van de ingebruikname.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source establishes both the completion of deployment and the subsequent months of commissioning. Calling deployment an important milestone is a reasonable characterization of that documented transition.","materiality":"Accurately states the piece’s main conclusion about the relationship between deployment and commissioning."}]}

